# A challenger after a VS match: a save that brings one (make_save.py)
# loads from the run's card, the opening movie and title screen pass, and
# VS Melee starts with Fox against a CPU on a random stage. The match is
# quit from the pause at once, a no contest that still counts: results,
# then the New challenger screen. The save is made beside the run, never
# committed:
#   python tools/a11y/make_save.py challenger jigglypuff
#   python tools/a11y/drive.py tools/a11y/challenger.drive --card=build/drive/challenger.gci
# For another challenger, name it to make_save.py (mewtwo, roy, ...); the
# script is the same.

wait '"Opening movie\. Press Start to skip\."' 60
press Start until '"Title screen\. Press Start\."' 20 1
sleep 1
press Start until '"Main Menu\. ' 20 1
sleep 1
press Down
wait '"VS\. Mode\. '
press A
wait '"VS\. Mode\. Melee\. '
sleep 0.3
press A
wait '"Character select\. Player 1, no character\.'
sleep 1
# Fox for player 1.
press DUp
wait ': "Player 1: closed"$'
press DUp
wait ': "Pichu"$'
press DUp
wait ': "Fox"$'
wait 'glide to "Fox" ended after \d+ frames: arrived'
press A
sleep 1
# Player 2 a CPU.
search ': "Player 2: closed"$' DDown*2 DRight*3 DLeft*3
wait 'glide to "Player 2: closed" ended'
press A until 'Ready to fight\. Press Start\.'
sleep 0.5
# Random stage, then quit from the pause: L, R, A and Start held together.
press Start
wait '"Stage select\. '
sleep 1
press Start
sleep 8
press Start
sleep 1
press L+R+A+Start 1000
press Start until '"Time Battle\. No contest\. ' 5 2
press Start
wait '"KOs and falls\. '
sleep 0.5
press Start
# The New challenger screen. Its line is the scene table's until the
# screen gets a reader of its own.
wait '"New challenger"$'
